From a0f30c0e9cc1bd832693957f65f44ff152e9fddf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kissshot <ttyinzg@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:08:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(trajectory): branch a child Session from any
 completed-turn record

The Trajectory view could only be read. Branching existed solely in the
chat view, on a turn's final message, so a decision point visible as a
tool call or an intermediate assistant step had no way to fork from it.

Each record whose source event belongs to a closed turn now carries a
hover branch control that forks through session.fork and opens the child.
Availability compares the record's source seq against the largest loaded
turn/end seq: the Host anchors the cut at the first turn/end at or after
that seq and refuses an anchor whose turn is still open, so a row past the
last completed turn offers no control rather than a failing one. The
control stops click and double-click propagation, which the row owns for
selection and folding.

ui-trajectory owns these rows and already injects sessions, so branchAt
extends its injected face rather than adding a package or a per-row slot
inside the virtualized table. Copy stays in the trajectory dictionary,
passed in as labels because this table renders fixed English column and
kind labels and takes no translate function.

Live pause needs no new control: the composer's stop already calls the
same session.cancel, which the Host performs with keepInbox: true.
